  "hints": [
    "Never run user code inside the web tier. Where do submissions go, and who runs them?",
    "Everyone reads the same few problems and the scoreboard: cache them. Editor assets belong on a CDN.",
    "CDN → LB (2) → API (4) → Redis (2) → Postgres (2); API → SQS → Judges (3) → NoSQL verdicts."
  ],
  "scoring": {
    "weights": {
      "performance": 0.35,
      "reliability": 0.3,
      "cost": 0.15,
      "architecture": 0.2
    },
    "latencyTargetMs": 40,
    "costBudget": 2800
  },
  "explanation": [
    "Judging is a queue-and-worker problem: accept the submission, enqueue it, return 'queued', and let sandboxed judges pull work at their own pace.",
    "Isolate every run (containers, Firecracker microVMs or services like E2B) with CPU, memory and time limits, and no network.",
    "Contest traffic is extremely hot on a few problems: cache statements and the scoreboard, and push static editor assets to a CDN."
  ]
